{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q4921678","formula":"C₁₂H₁₄N₄O₄S","hill":"C12H14N4O4S","elements":["H","C","N","O","S"],"composition":{"C":12.0,"H":14.0,"N":4.0,"O":4.0,"S":1.0},"names":{"en":"Sulfadimethoxine","ru":"Сульфадиметоксин","uk":"Сульфадиметоксин"},"descriptions":{"en":"Sulfadimethoxine (or sulphadimethoxine, trade names Di-Methox or Albon) is a long-lasting sulfonamide antimicrobial medication used in veterinary medicine. It is used to treat many infections, including respiratory, urinary tract, enteric, and soft tissue infections and can be given as a standalone or combined with ormetoprim to broaden the target range. Like all sulfamides, sulfadimethoxine inhibits bacterial synthesis of folic acid by acting as a competitive inhibitor against PABA. It is the most common drug prescribed to dogs who have coccidiosis.","ru":"Сульфадиметоксин — антибактериальное средство, сульфаниламидный препарат длительного действия.","uk":"Сульфадиметокси́н — синтетичний антибактеріальний препарат з групи сульфаніламідних препаратів для перорального застосування."},"fame":15,"pubchemCid":5323,"mass":310.33,"charge":0,"smiles":"COC1=NC(=NC(=C1)NS(=O)(=O)C2=CC=C(C=C2)N)OC","inchikey":"ZZORFUFYDOWNEF-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"4-amino-N-(2,6-dimethoxypyrimidin-4-yl)benzenesulfonamide","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"5323","atoms":35,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-1.27,"y":-2.21,"z":-0.546,"el":"S"},{"x":-2.24,"y":-2.869,"z":-1.413,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.774,"y":-2.925,"z":0.623,"el":"O"},{"x":2.135,"y":2.621,"z":-1.306,"el":"O"},{"x":3.39,"y":-0.749,"z":1.618,"el":"O"},{"x":0.058,"y":-1.703,"z":-1.519,"el":"N"},{"x":1.739,"y":-1.222,"z":0.065,"el":"N"},{"x":-3.639,"y":2.944,"z":1.237,"el":"N"},{"x":2.778,"y":0.95,"z":0.168,"el":"N"},{"x":-1.967,"y":-0.697,"z":-0.022,"